Optional lifestyle / editorial imagery. The design does not depend on these —
every editorial block is art-directed so it looks deliberate with or without a
photograph — but these files fill the slots the pages ask for.

| File | Used by | Crop |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `hero.webp` | home — hero | 2200 × 1300 |
| `craft.webp` | home — Our craft | 1600 × 1000 |
| `cat-her.webp` | home — shop-by-family tile | 900 × 1200 |
| `cat-him.webp` | home — shop-by-family tile | 900 × 1200 |
| `cat-unisex.webp` | home — shop-by-family tile | 900 × 1200 |
| `cat-recreate.webp` | home — shop-by-family tile | 900 × 1200 |
| `recreate-steps.webp` | recreate — Four steps | 1200 × 1500 |
| `story.webp` | atelier — Our story | 1400 × 1750 |
| `in-person.webp` | atelier — In person | 1600 × 1000 |

Replace any of them with your own photograph of the same name, or drop new files
in and point the markup at them. `node tools/.fetch-stock-images.mjs` refetches
and re-encodes the current stock set as WebP (Pexels, free to use, no attribution
required).
